{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Requirement Elicitation Process and Techniques"}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to discuss requirement techniques."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Learning Outcome"}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Participates in simple conversations or simulated situations about the communicative topics for this level through grammar and vocabulary structures.  Recognizes simple ideas on requirement reports, tools for Object Oriented Programming, and other basic programming tools."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Read again the text about requirement elicitation process."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Invent a dialogue where you explain what requirement elicitation process and techniques are."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the dialogue aloud and correct your pronunciation with your instructor."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I read the information about requirement elicitation process and requirement."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I create an original dialogue."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my work with my instructor."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Infinitives of Purpose"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We can use infinitives of verbs to show our mission or goal of what we are doing.   "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The preposition <span class=\"strong\">to</span> expresses the reason we have for doing something, we can use it at the beginning or in the middle of a sentence.<br /><br />  Examples: <br /> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">To</span> improve customer service we need a new software. <br /> I'm sorting out the requirements <span class=\"strong\">to</span> start the analysis.  </span><br /><br />  To add emphasis in a formal way, you can use in order and so as before the to-infinitive.<br /><br />  Example: <br /> <span class=\"italic\">He makes a survey <span class=\"strong\">in order to</span>  know financial departments' opinion.<br /> Developers gather all the information <span class=\"strong\">so as to</span> know the expected results.</span><br /><br />  Remember that the verb with to is the one that shows the purpose of the actions, those actions can come either in simple present or present continuous. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Purpose</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Actions</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">To improve the system</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">we are changing the software.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Actions</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Purpose</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I always make a back-up copy</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">to protect my files. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Requirement elicitation is the process of communicating with the clients, end-users, and all the participants in the development of the software in order to find out the requirements for the system."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Surveys are useful to query stakeholders about their expectations from the upcoming system."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Questionnaires are a technique designed to gather customers' requirements."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Troubleshooting and Giving Advice"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you troubleshoot a problem, means you solved the problem and everything is fine. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you want to give an advice you usually use the modal verb should, but if the advice becomes stronger, you can use the modals <span class=\"strong\">have to</span> or <span class=\"strong\">must</span>.<br /><br /> Examples:<br /> <span class=\"italic\">You should restart the computer.</span> <br /><br />  Notice that the verb after \u201cshould\u201d (restart) comes in the base form. <br /><br />  Another expression you can use to give advice is \u201cwhy don't you\u201d this means <span class=\"italic\">\u201cyou should try doing this, maybe it works\u201d</span> .<br /><br />  Examples: <br /> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Why don't you</span> reboot the system?<br /> <span class=\"strong\">Why don't you</span> run the antivirus?</span> <br /><br />  Notice that the expression \u201cwhy don't you\u201d is actually a question in simple present, so you make it just as any other question in the present. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Useful Sentences to Talk About Troubleshooting and Advice</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Did you initialize the drive?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Did you verify software compatibility?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> You should download a data recovery software to help you. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You should back up all the restored data.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Why don't you try using the default password?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Why don't you run some tests to make sure everything is stable?</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You should back up all the collected data, you don't want to lose all that information."}, {"type": "example", "content": "In case you forget to backup you should download a data recovery software to help you."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "workflow"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the procedure that defines actors, actions, decisions and results"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Developers visit the client's work place and observe the workflow in general and how workers deal with execution problems."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob04aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "draw out"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to discover"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Some important techniques to collect and draw out software requirements.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob04aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "stage"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in this case, a step or point of a process"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are four stages in the process of eliciting requirements."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob04aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "query"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to question"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Surveys are useful to query stakeholders about their expectations from the upcoming system."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob04aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "upcoming"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "expected "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Surveys are useful to query stakeholders about their expectations from the upcoming system."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob04aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "shortcoming"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a disadvantage"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Questionnaires are a technique designed to gather customers' requirements, with the shortcoming that if they leave out of a question any issue, they won't take that issue into account."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob04aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n3le01ob04re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n3le01ob04re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "We are going to discuss requirement elicitation, and some important techniques to collect and draw out software requirements.\nRequirement elicitation is the process of communicating with the clients, end-users, and all the participants in the development of the software to find out the requirements for the system."}, {"time": "22000", "image": "enpe8n3le01ob04re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "There are four stages in the process of eliciting requirements: requirement gathering, which consists on discussing with the clients and users to know their desires about the software. Requirement organization, it's when the developers arrange requirements in order of priority. Negotiation and discussion, it's when the developers discuss and negotiate the requirements with clients in case there is conflict or ambiguity among requirements to finally document requirements. You should back up all the collected data, you don't want to lose all that information; in case you forget to backup you should download a data recovery software to help you."}, {"time": "65000", "image": "enpe8n3le01ob04re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "There are some important techniques to gather the requirements you need to recognize: Interviews are a strong way to collect requirements, they can be structured, with close definite questions, or non-structured with open flexible questions; interviews can also be written or oral, one-to-one or in groups. Surveys are useful to query stakeholders about their expectations from the upcoming system. Questionnaires are a technique designed to gather customers' requirements, with the shortcoming that if they leave out of a question any issue, they won't take that issue into account.\nBrainstorming is a technique in which participants hold a debate about the system; developers record their opinions for further requirement analysis. There is also an observation technique, in which developers visit the client's work place and observe the workflow in general and how workers deal with execution problems.\nRequirement elicitation is a long complex process, developers use all those tools to decide on the best software system for each company."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n3le01ob04re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can understand what requirement elicitation process is."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can recognize the techniques of requirements elicitation."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain what requirement elicitation process and techniques are."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What aspects do you consider important when collecting requirements for software design? Why?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What are some common demands from clients when implementing a new software system? "}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "The best way to identify the requirements."}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "img_path": ""}, {"stimuli_ids": [1], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " How to <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">elicit</span> requirements"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Content"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type":